    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d880">

                <pb facs="0822" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/7899: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-01-24T17:00:00+03:00">January 24, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 25—8:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. For the Secretary and Under Secretary only. Both Turkish and British
                    informants assured me that the military consultations reported in my No.
                        10<anchor n="3" xml:id="d880-f1"/> are proceeding very satisfactorily.</p>
                <p>I have reason to believe that the Turkish Government has made clear its intention
                    to fight in any of the following eventualities: first, <pb facs="0823" n="815"
                        xml:id="pg815"/> an attack upon its own territory from any quarter; second,
                    a Bulgarian attack on Greece; third, a German advance into Bulgaria; and fourth,
                    an Axis advance threatening seizure of Saloniki. There appears to have been no
                    decision yet reached as to the case of a German advance through Yugoslavia not
                    directly menacing Saloniki.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Minister<anchor n="4" xml:id="d880-f2"/> today reaffirmed to me his
                    confident conviction that Bulgaria will not, at any rate willingly, allow the
                    passage of German [troops?] through her territory.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
